WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.725
This video walks through escape at Dix River Stone.

00:07.725 --> 00:10.412
The map here is a simplified trace of the Dix River

00:10.412 --> 00:14.388
Level 1 escapeway map. The Level 2 map shows mostly

00:14.388 --> 00:17.325
planned workings, so its routes change as the headings

00:17.325 --> 00:21.113
advance. The map posted at the mine always governs.

00:21.113 --> 00:23.250
Your instructor will show you the current maps

00:23.250 --> 00:25.725
and walk the actual escapeways with you.

00:26.844 --> 00:29.594
Dix River is an underground limestone mine with

00:29.594 --> 00:33.706
two levels. For years after Allen took over in 2018,

00:33.706 --> 00:37.157
production was mostly surface drill and blast.

00:37.157 --> 00:40.194
Surface mining has now stopped, and active production

00:40.194 --> 00:43.494
is header mining, room-and-pillar, on Level 1 and

00:43.494 --> 00:46.782
Level 2. Shot rock is hauled to the primary crusher

00:46.782 --> 00:47.944
on the surface.

00:49.074 --> 00:51.487
That change matters for escape. An underground

00:51.487 --> 00:54.274
mine that's growing changes every week.

00:54.274 --> 00:57.487
New headings open, and the escape routes get longer

00:57.487 --> 01:00.112
and change with them. So the map you saw in training

01:00.112 --> 01:02.474
may not be the map that's posted today.

01:02.474 --> 01:04.999
Check the posted map whenever you pass it,

01:04.999 --> 01:07.837
and when your work area moves, walk the escapeways

01:07.837 --> 01:08.549
again.

01:09.672 --> 01:12.347
Above ground, shot rock from the mine is hauled

01:12.347 --> 01:14.722
to the primary crusher, then conveyed from the

01:14.722 --> 01:18.197
surge silo to the secondary plant, where it's crushed,

01:18.197 --> 01:21.309
screened and stockpiled. The speed limit on site

01:21.309 --> 01:24.409
is fifteen miles per hour, traffic keeps right,

01:24.409 --> 01:26.359
and haul trucks have the right of way.

01:26.359 --> 01:28.697
When you come out of the portal in an emergency,

01:28.697 --> 01:31.434
you're stepping into that traffic. Stay alert,

01:31.434 --> 01:32.972
and stay on the walkways.

01:36.298 --> 01:38.498
Check in on the tag board in the breakroom every

01:38.498 --> 01:41.460
shift, and tag out every time you come out.

01:41.460 --> 01:44.160
Never tag for anyone else. Then know which level

01:44.160 --> 01:46.885
you're on today, Level 1 or Level 2,

01:46.885 --> 01:50.035
and your work area. At Dix River, the escapeways

01:50.035 --> 01:52.773
and maps differ by level, so the level decides

01:52.773 --> 01:55.660
your way out. It's the first line on your Dix River

01:55.660 --> 01:56.935
emergency card.

01:58.072 --> 02:02.210
Before you go underground, check your W65 self-rescuer.

02:02.210 --> 02:04.997
Everyone underground wears or carries one.

02:04.997 --> 02:07.185
If wearing it would be hazardous for a particular

02:07.185 --> 02:10.485
job, it can be no more than twenty-five feet away.

02:10.485 --> 02:12.873
If you work on mobile equipment, it can be kept

02:12.873 --> 02:15.273
where you can reach it easily on the machine.

02:15.273 --> 02:18.097
Module 3 covered how to inspect and put on the

02:18.097 --> 02:21.410
W65. If anything about yours looks wrong,

02:21.410 --> 02:23.148
swap it out before you go in.

02:26.462 --> 02:29.424
Every underground mine must have at least two separate

02:29.424 --> 02:32.424
escapeways to the surface from its lowest levels,

02:32.424 --> 02:35.850
placed so damage to one doesn't block the other.

02:35.850 --> 02:38.424
Learn the primary and the secondary from your work

02:38.424 --> 02:41.512
area on your level. On the maps, both are marked

02:41.512 --> 02:44.562
with green arrows. A P in the arrow's circle means

02:44.562 --> 02:48.212
primary, and an S means secondary. If someone is

02:48.212 --> 02:50.462
hurt underground, they come out by the primary

02:50.462 --> 02:53.387
escapeway, and any miner can call for help and

02:53.387 --> 02:55.149
meet the ambulance at the portal.

02:56.264 --> 02:58.501
Walk both escapeways from your level with your

02:58.501 --> 03:00.864
instructor before you work there alone.

03:00.864 --> 03:03.276
Pay attention to how long it takes and where the

03:03.276 --> 03:05.989
route goes from one level to the surface.

03:05.989 --> 03:09.614
Your W65 is there to get you out. It filters carbon

03:09.614 --> 03:12.701
monoxide, but it makes no oxygen, so knowing the

03:12.701 --> 03:16.214
route well and moving steadily to fresh air matters.

03:16.214 --> 03:18.639
And whenever mining moves your work area,

03:18.639 --> 03:20.814
walk the routes from the new spot too.

03:21.938 --> 03:24.201
Escape routes are inspected regularly,

03:24.201 --> 03:27.125
kept travelable, and marked with signs that clearly

03:27.125 --> 03:30.375
point the way out. Dix River has a written escape

03:30.375 --> 03:33.451
and evacuation plan, and parts of the map are posted

03:33.451 --> 03:36.313
where people gather underground. On the maps,

03:36.313 --> 03:38.951
escapeways are marked with green arrows.

03:38.951 --> 03:42.113
Underground, the primary escapeway has white reflectors

03:42.113 --> 03:45.375
on the ribs and the secondary has blue reflectors,

03:45.375 --> 03:47.875
with reflective signs and arrows.

03:49.004 --> 03:51.579
Stone is stockpiled underground here as well as

03:51.579 --> 03:54.479
on the surface. Stockpiles and parked equipment

03:54.479 --> 03:57.267
must never block an escapeway. If they do,

03:57.267 --> 03:58.179
report it.

03:59.294 --> 04:02.956
At Dix River, the escape map is posted in the breakroom

04:02.956 --> 04:05.369
and in a covered box on the side of the plant trailer

04:05.369 --> 04:08.056
on the flat. Stop and study it before your first

04:08.056 --> 04:10.294
shift, so you know your way out before you ever

04:10.294 --> 04:11.094
need it.

04:12.224 --> 04:15.462
If smoke, fire, or fallen rock blocks the primary

04:15.462 --> 04:18.712
escapeway, turn back and take the secondary.

04:18.712 --> 04:21.124
Stay together. If you get turned around,

04:21.124 --> 04:23.512
stop at an intersection and look for the direction

04:23.512 --> 04:26.474
signs. Header mining makes tall openings,

04:26.474 --> 04:28.849
and in smoke the ribs and pillars can all look

04:28.849 --> 04:31.612
alike. Landmarks you learned on your walk,

04:31.612 --> 04:34.399
like a turn at a particular intersection or a change

04:34.399 --> 04:37.299
in the road surface, help you keep your bearings.

04:40.626 --> 04:43.663
At Dix River, the underground fire warning is stench

04:43.663 --> 04:46.788
gas released into the intake fan. Warnings also

04:46.788 --> 04:49.901
come by radio and strobe lights. At the first sign

04:49.901 --> 04:52.926
of smoke, a CO alarm, or stench gas,

04:52.926 --> 04:56.139
put on your W65 self-rescuer right away and head

04:56.139 --> 04:59.439
out. The hot, dry air it gives you is normal.

04:59.439 --> 05:00.326
Keep it on.

05:01.452 --> 05:04.677
On the surface, the CB radio and the scale house

05:04.677 --> 05:07.327
are on channel 16. Your instructor will tell you

05:07.327 --> 05:10.065
the call words to use in an emergency.

05:11.203 --> 05:13.565
Once you're out, go to your gathering point and

05:13.565 --> 05:16.440
report to the person in charge so you're counted.

05:16.440 --> 05:18.428
Don't go back in unless you're told to.

05:18.428 --> 05:21.415
There's no designated refuge chamber at Dix River,

05:21.415 --> 05:24.290
so the plan is to get out. Evacuation drills are

05:24.290 --> 05:26.990
held at least every six months, and they're your

05:26.990 --> 05:30.028
chance to walk the real route under time pressure.

05:30.028 --> 05:33.202
At Dix River, the gathering point is the tag board.

05:34.333 --> 05:37.120
To sum up for Dix River. Tag in, and know your

05:37.120 --> 05:40.095
level and work area. Know both escapeways from

05:40.095 --> 05:42.995
where you work, and recheck the posted map as the

05:42.995 --> 05:47.095
mine grows. At the first warning, put on your W65

05:47.095 --> 05:49.633
and get out. Then go to the gathering point and

05:49.633 --> 05:52.433
be counted. Fill in your emergency card with your

05:52.433 --> 05:55.245
instructor before your first shift underground.

05:56.370 --> 05:59.533
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

05:59.533 --> 06:01.033
override this video.
